I'm working on my 12th role on NAO, Caveman.  After that, I only have 
Ranger, then I'll have beat the game on NAO with every role (although, 
possibly, not every combo).

I'm in the mines, and I step into a narrow corridor and *click*, 
*rumble* trigger a rolling boulder trap.  Ouch.  The boulder flies down 
the corridor, and smacks into me.  Dusting myself off, I continue.  I go 
two steps, when I see a forest centaur step into the corridor at the far 
end.  I'm level 7 or 8, and I have a +1 club.  *gulp*.  It advances 
menacingly.  I step back until I'm backed up against the trap.  Nowhere 
to run to... no teleport options, no digging options.  What do I do?

I trigger the trap :)

Boulder whizzes by me (yay!)... Boulder smacks into centaur!
I take another step back, the centaur follows, right onto the trap
boulder kills the centaur, boulder whizzes by me again :)  Haa-haa.

Later, a nymph snuck up on me and yanked my wand of cold.  Somewhat 
painfully, I killed her the same way.  Stepped in between her and a 
wall, she zaps me, hits me twice, then dies to her own bolt of cold.

I survived all that, now I'm out of the mines, got a BoH randomly 
generated, did Soko, got the reflection variant (yay!), and have an AC 
of -3.  Feeling.... safer.  Kinda midgamish.  If/when I get a decent 
weapon, and relieve a grey dragon of it's scales, I'll be veery comfortable.

Wish me luck!

